    {
      "path": "scripts/scene_host_proxy.py",
      "content": "The reconcile log prints the *pre-re-post* value of `cur`, but `cur` is never updated to `\"DONE\"` after `backend.step(..., \"DONE\", ...)` succeeds. So even on the confirmed path the message reads e.g. `re-reported \u003crun_id\u003e/REGISTER='RUNNING'-\u003eDONE` (or `'None'-\u003eDONE`), contradicting the literal `-\u003eDONE` suffix and making post-fault reconcile audits mislead: an operator scanning logs for `'DONE'-\u003eDONE` / an actual `DONE` source state won't find it. The preceding `if cur == \"DONE\": return` guarantees this print only runs right after attempting the DONE re-post, so it should reflect the DONE intent.",
      "suggestion_code": "        if cur not in (\"DONE\", \"FAILED\"):\n            backend.step(run_id, name, \"DONE\", attempt, lease_token, error=str(rec.get(\"detail\") or \"\"))\n            cur = \"DONE\"\n        print(f\"16B terminal step re-reported {run_id}/{name}={cur!r}\", flush=True)",
